1. src/locks.ts is a modified version of ONLYOFFICE Docs: the lock rules of
   the server's DocService/sources/DocsCoServer.js (Docs 9.4.0: getLock,
   _checkLockExcel, _checkLockPresentation, compareExcelBlock,
   comparePresentationBlock, _recalcLockArray, _addRecalcIndex,
   CRecalcIndex, and the in-memory editorData's addLocksNX), translated to
   TypeScript and changed to run on a session log instead of a database.
   Modified by BRF Tech on 2026-10-08.
   Portions Copyright (C) Ascensio System SIA. ONLYOFFICE licenses that code
   under the GNU AGPL version 3 only, with additional terms under section 7,
   so this file is AGPL-3.0-only.

2. src/bridge.ts and src/protocol.ts answer the editor in the Document
   Server's protocol (the names and numbers of sdkjs common/docscoapi.js and
   DocsCoServer.js, 9.4), so the editor runs unchanged.

3. The editor files the bundle carries (web-apps, sdkjs, the fonts) are
   ONLYOFFICE's, taken from ONLYOFFICE's official Document Server image
   (docker.io/onlyoffice/documentserver) at the release, image tag and
   digest pinned in upstream/onlyoffice.json - today ONLYOFFICE Docs 9.4.0,
   build 9.4.0.129; their source is ONLYOFFICE's sdkjs and web-apps at tag
   v9.4.0.129. scripts/extract-editor.sh builds the bundle from that image;
   upstream/editor.lock.json lists every file in it with its SHA-256. The
   fonts are generated from ONLYOFFICE's core-fonts the way the image does
   on its first start; each font family's license files, and the notices
   inside its fonts, travel with them (core-fonts-licenses/ in the bundle).
   All of it is under ONLYOFFICE's license (AGPL-3.0 with additional terms)
   and the fonts' own licenses; every copyright, license and origin notice
   they ship is kept.

   Changes this project makes to those files, by BRF Tech, 2026-10-08
   (each one listed with its file in upstream/editor.lock.json, "changed"
   and "added", and in the bundle as filex/CHANGES.txt):
     - the HTML pages of web-apps: each inline script moved, unchanged, into
       a file next to its page (index.inline-1.js, ...) and loaded from the
       same place; the stylesheet loaded as media="print" with an onload
       handler loaded as media="all"; a first script added that gives the
       page an in-memory localStorage where the browser refuses one, and
       takes navigator.serviceWorker away where reading it throws
       (filex/storage.js, this project's own);
     - web-apps/apps/api/documents/api.js is api.js.tpl, with the cache tag
       left as a placeholder;
     - ONLYOFFICE's license/*.license files and the editors' interface
       templates (web-apps/apps/*/main/{app,lib}/template/*.template) carry
       a .txt extension, and the Document Server's blank documents
       (document-templates/new/default/new.docx, .xlsx, .pptx) a .bin one;
       their content is unchanged;
     - parts the app does not use are left out (help pages, the PDF and
       Visio editors, the embedded and forms apps, the macro editor,
       dictionaries, asm.js fallbacks, the server's script snapshots, the
       per-theme thumbnails, some fonts); the lock file names each kind and
