4. The x2t WebAssembly build (x2t/x2t.js, x2t/x2t.wasm in the app's
   bundle) is ONLYOFFICE's converter, x2t, built by this project from
   ONLYOFFICE core (https://github.com/ONLYOFFICE/core) at tag v9.4.0.129,
   the editor files' own tag, with emscripten. scripts/x2t/ builds it
   (build.sh, Dockerfile, steps.sh) and upstream/onlyoffice.json pins it
   ("x2t": every source by its commit, the toolchain by its digest, the two
   files by their SHA-256). It is a modified version of ONLYOFFICE core.
   The changes are made at build time, by the patches in scripts/x2t/patches/
   and two files of this project (scripts/x2t/main1.cpp, appended to
   X2tConverter/src/main.cpp, and scripts/x2t/pre-js.js, put before the
   module's JavaScript):
     - 01-cryptpad-wasm.patch: CryptPad's changes to ONLYOFFICE core for
       WebAssembly, from https://github.com/cryptpad/onlyoffice-x2t-wasm
       (AGPL-3.0-or-later; its core/ at tag v9.3.0+0 against ONLYOFFICE
       core v9.3.0.140, its build recipe at commit
       7debf5e6d6d4f19874d764cd34446f7e63c6bc32): the build files of the
       libraries x2t links, doctrenderer without a JavaScript engine
       (DesktopEditor/doctrenderer/*_empty.cpp, CryptPad's), two functions
       of HtmlFile2 renamed, the FB2 converter left out, x2t's memory limit
       left out, pdf.bin read from beside the document. Ported to core
       v9.4.0.129 by BRF Tech on 2026-10-10, with the parts that do not
       apply there left out (README.md, "x2t, the converter");
     - 02-wasm-link-flags.patch (BRF Tech, 2026-10-10): two linker flags
       emscripten's linker does not know are not passed to it, and HEIF
       pictures (libheif, not built for WebAssembly) are left out;
     - 03-unicode-utf32.patch (BRF Tech, 2026-10-10): UnicodeConverter
       turns wchar_t (UTF-32 here) into ICU's UTF-16 with ICU's UTF-32
       functions; through u_strFromWCS every letter outside ASCII of a txt
       or csv lost all but its low byte in the WebAssembly build;
     - 04-starmath.patch (BRF Tech, 2026-10-10): x2t links ONLYOFFICE's
       StarMath converter (OdfFile/Reader/Converter/StarMath2OOXML), which
       CryptPad's build leaves out and without which an ODF formula stops
       the module;
     - 05-frame-anchor.patch (BRF Tech, 2026-10-10): the ODF reader reads a
       frame's anchor (text:anchor-type) from the frame whether or not the
       frame has a graphic style (OdfFile/Reader/Format/draw_frame_docx.cpp);
       a frame without a style lost its anchor and became a floating shape.
   The build is CryptPad's recipe (its Dockerfile and embuild.sh) carried
   over to that tag. The third-party code ONLYOFFICE core builds into x2t
   is fetched by core's own scripts at the commits they name, and keeps its
   license (core's 3DPARTY.md); it is a part of the third-party code the
   Document Server's own x2t carries, whose license files travel in the
   bundle (editor/license/, editor/3rd-Party.txt). The build adds:
   Boost 1.84.0 (Boost Software License 1.0), the headers of OpenSSL
   1.1.1f (no OpenSSL code is linked), hyphen (MPL 1.1, GPL 2.0 or LGPL
   2.1) and emscripten 4.0.11's runtime, C and C++ libraries and ICU 68.2
   port (MIT, the University of Illinois/NCSA license, Apache 2.0 with the
   LLVM exception, the Unicode license). Releases 0.3.0 and 0.2.0 carry
   this build (x2t v9.4.0.129+2); release 0.1.1 carried it without
   05-frame-anchor.patch (x2t v9.4.0.129+1); release 0.1.0 carried
   CryptPad's own build of x2t (release v9.3.2+3) unchanged.

